{"name":"Dried Goldenrod","hex":"#e2a829","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dried","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without water or moisture, said of something that has previously been wet or moist; resulting from the process of drying.","Usually of foods: cured, preserved by drying."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of dry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dried"},{"term":"goldenrod","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tall-stemmed plant principally from genus Solidago (also Oligoneuron), usually with clusters of small yellow flowers.","A golden-yellow colour, like that of the goldenrod plant."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a golden-yellow colour, like that of the goldenrod plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goldenrod"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drying","blocks":[{"text":"Drying is a mass transfer process consisting of the removal of water or another solvent by evaporation from a solid, semi-solid or liquid. This process is often used as a final production step before selling or packaging products. To be considered \"dried\", the final product must be solid, in the form of a continuous sheet, long pieces, particles or powder. A source of heat and an agent to remove the vapor produced by the process are often involved. In bioproducts like food, grains, and pharmaceuticals like vaccines, the solvent to be removed is almost invariably water. Desiccation may be synonymous with drying or considered an extreme form of drying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Raumluft_waeschetrockner.jpg/330px-Raumluft_waeschetrockner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drying"},{"title":"Goldenrod","blocks":[{"text":"Goldenrod is a common name for many species of flowering plants in the sunflower family, Asteraceae, commonly in reference to the genus Solidago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Solidago_nemoralis.jpg/330px-Solidago_nemoralis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldenrod"},{"title":"Goldenrod (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Goldenrod is a color that resembles that of the goldenrod plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Goldenrods_in_Fountain_County%2C_Indiana.png/330px-Goldenrods_in_Fountain_County%2C_Indiana.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldenrod_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg/500px-Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg/1280px-Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg/500px-Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drying of fish in Lofoten in the production of stockfish","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Euthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG/500px-Euthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Euthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG/1280px-Euthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Euthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG/500px-Euthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Euthamia graminifolia, grass-leaved goldenrod","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEuthamia_graminifolia_001.JPG"}],"sounds":{"dried":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg/En-us-dried.ogg.mp3"}],"goldenrod":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-goldenrod.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/85/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-goldenrod.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-goldenrod.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/85/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-goldenrod.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-goldenrod.wav.ogg"}]}}}